    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 11 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field (formatted as `LastName, FirstName`) for owners with two small changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since the DTOs (`OwnerDto`) are generated from this spec at build time, this creates the field on the response object. `readOnly: true` keeps it out of request bodies.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the stored entity names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause the value is derived in the mapper (used by the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated` responder and the GET-owner path), it's computed from the persisted names rather than the raw request \u2014 exactly as the spec requires. The new `Cp05Tests` passes, as does the rest of the suite.",
